id: pm-rust-23ps
title: Give concurrent claim-next acceptance an explicit writer wait budget
description: "The aggregate gate observed a valid lock_conflict after 3007ms in the existing two-writer claim-next acceptance test, while the isolated rerun passed. That test expects both writers to succeed but inherits the finite default wait. Configure an explicit fixture wait budget for both replay trackers; retain the two competing writers, distinct-item assertions, serial oracle replay and every gate threshold."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 3
tags[2]: concurrency,conformance
