comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-16T19:20:30.044Z",codex-agent,"Observed one aggregate failure: beta received lock_conflict after waiting 3007ms for alpha. The isolated regression passed with the same source. Both replay trackers now declare locks.wait_ms=30000 for this two-success acceptance scenario. Competing native processes, distinct identities, session ordering and exact serial oracle artifact checks remain in place; production defaults and all gate thresholds are unchanged."
  "2026-10-16T20:10:28.532Z",codex-agent,The linked isolated competing-writer acceptance passed after explicitly configuring the fixture wait budget. The aggregate gate will rerun every original assertion on this source; no production locking behavior changed.
  "2026-10-16T21:40:24.231Z",codex-agent,"The fixture-only 30-second wait budget passes isolated linked pm test execution and the final clean aggregate gate: 374 normal tests and 374 instrumented tests, with all four unchanged coverage floors at 100 percent. The competing workers, distinct-item assertions, session ordering and exact serial oracle replay remain intact. Production wait defaults remain unchanged. This Chore remains in progress; its claim is released for review."
